=== layout: subsection

# Reading Chromosome Addresses

=== layout: one-panel

# Read an Address

@body

[*Gene address*]{color=#24578F}: like a book's library address

{table-style=comparison text-align=left padding="3pt 10pt"}
| [Part]{text-align=center} | What It Names | [Example]{text-align=center} |
| --- | --- | --- |
| [*Chromosome*]{color=#D40000 font-size=28pt text-align=center} | Which chromosome? | [*7*]{color=#D40000 font-size=30pt text-align=center} |
| [*Arm*]{color=#B74300 font-size=28pt text-align=center} | Short p or long q? | [*q*]{color=#B74300 font-size=30pt text-align=center} |
| [*Region*]{color=#007A00 font-size=28pt text-align=center} | Which region of that arm? | [*3*]{color=#007A00 font-size=30pt text-align=center} |
| [*Band*]{color=#003FFF font-size=28pt text-align=center} | Which band in that region? | [*1*]{color=#003FFF font-size=30pt text-align=center} |
| [*Subband*]{color=#A719DB font-size=28pt text-align=center} | Which part of that band? | [*.2*]{color=#A719DB font-size=30pt text-align=center} |

=== layout: one-panel

# Try It: The CFTR Address

@body

*CFTR*: *7q31.2*

- Which [*chromosome*]{color=#D40000}?
- Which [*arm*]{color=#B74300}?
- Which [*region*]{color=#007A00}?
- Which [*band*]{color=#003FFF}?
- Which [*subband*]{color=#A719DB}?

=== layout: two-panels

# CFTR: Read Each Part

@left

{table-style=comparison text-align=left padding="3pt 10pt"}
| [Address Part]{text-align=center} | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| [*7*]{color=#D40000 font-size=32pt text-align=center} | Chromosome 7 |
| [*q*]{color=#B74300 font-size=32pt text-align=center} | Long arm |
| [*3*]{color=#007A00 font-size=32pt text-align=center} | Region 3 |
| [*1*]{color=#003FFF font-size=32pt text-align=center} | Band 1 |
| [*.2*]{color=#A719DB font-size=32pt text-align=center} | Subband 2 |

@right

![Original chromosome 7 band-location figure showing region 3, band 1, and subband 2 at CFTR address 7q31.2](assets/lect10c-chromo_nomenclature/image_012.png)

@citation

https://medlineplus.gov/genetics/understanding/howgeneswork/genelocation/

