=== layout: one-panel

# Nearer or Farther?

@body

[*Higher band numbers*]{color=#003FFF}: farther from the centromere

{table-style=comparison}
| Same Arm | Nearer the Centromere | Farther from the Centromere |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Chromosome 14, q arm | [[*14*]{color=#D40000}[*q*]{color=#B74300}[*2*]{color=#007A00}[*1*]{color=#003FFF}]{font-size=32pt text-align=center} | [[*14*]{color=#D40000}[*q*]{color=#B74300}[*2*]{color=#007A00}[*2*]{color=#003FFF}]{font-size=32pt text-align=center} |

- Compare [*chromosome*]{color=#D40000} and [*arm*]{color=#B74300} first
- Then compare [*region*]{color=#007A00}, [*band*]{color=#003FFF}, and [*subband*]{color=#A719DB}
- [*Band label*]{color=#003FFF}: address, not distance in cM

@citation

https://medlineplus.gov/genetics/understanding/howgeneswork/genelocation/

=== layout: multiple-choice

@question

[On chromosome *17q*, which band is most distal (farthest from the centromere)?]{color=#000000}

- A. [*17*]{color=#D40000}[*q*]{color=#B74300}[*3*]{color=#007A00}[*6*]{color=#003FFF}
- B. [*17*]{color=#D40000}[*q*]{color=#B74300}[*3*]{color=#007A00}[*6*]{color=#003FFF}[*.3*]{color=#A719DB}
- C. [*17*]{color=#D40000}[*q*]{color=#B74300}[*1*]{color=#007A00}[*1*]{color=#003FFF}
- D. [*17*]{color=#D40000}[*q*]{color=#B74300}[*3*]{color=#007A00}[*4*]{color=#003FFF}[*.1*]{color=#A719DB}
- E. [*17*]{color=#D40000}[*q*]{color=#B74300}[*4*]{color=#007A00}[*1*]{color=#003FFF}[*.3*]{color=#A719DB}

[*Numbering practice: schematic labels*]{color=#24578F}

@answer

E. [*17*]{color=#D40000}[*q*]{color=#B74300}[*4*]{color=#007A00}[*1*]{color=#003FFF}[*.3*]{color=#A719DB}

=== layout: one-panel

# Band Order: Answer

@body

- Same chromosome and arm: [*17*]{color=#D40000}[*q*]{color=#B74300}
- [*Region*]{color=#007A00} first: [*4*]{color=#007A00} farther out than [*3*]{color=#007A00} or [*1*]{color=#007A00}
- [*Region 4*]{color=#007A00}: [*17*]{color=#D40000}[*q*]{color=#B74300}[*4*]{color=#007A00}[*1*]{color=#003FFF}[*.3*]{color=#A719DB}
- [*Answer: E.*]{color=#007A00} [*17*]{color=#D40000}[*q*]{color=#B74300}[*4*]{color=#007A00}[*1*]{color=#003FFF}[*.3*]{color=#A719DB}

*Schematic labels; not a real chromosome 17 band map*

=== layout: subsection

# Reading a Karyotype

=== layout: one-panel

# Three Parts of a Simple Karyotype

@body

{table-style=comparison text-align=left}
| [Part]{text-align=center} | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| [*47*]{color=#D40000 font-size=36pt text-align=center} | Number of chromosomes |
| [*XY*]{color=#B74300 font-size=36pt text-align=center} | Sex-chromosome complement |
| [*+21*]{color=#003FFF font-size=36pt text-align=center} | Extra copy of chromosome 21 |

- [*+21*]{color=#003FFF}: extra *whole chromosome 21*
- [*7*]{color=#D40000}[*q*]{color=#B74300}[*3*]{color=#007A00}[*1*]{color=#003FFF}[*.2*]{color=#A719DB}: chromosome address

@citation

https://medlineplus.gov/genetics/condition/down-syndrome/

=== layout: multiple-choice

@question

[What does *47,XY,+21* describe?]{color=#000000}

- A. XX with two extra copies of chromosome 21
- B. XY with a partial deletion of chromosome 21
- C. XY with an extra pair of chromosome 21
- D. XX with one extra copy of chromosome 21
- E. XY with one extra copy of chromosome 21

@answer

E. XY with one extra copy of chromosome 21

=== layout: one-panel

# Karyotype: Answer

@body

- [*47*]{color=#D40000}: one more than 46
- [*XY*]{color=#B74300}: sex-chromosome complement
- [*+21*]{color=#003FFF}: one extra chromosome 21
- [*Answer: E*]{color=#007A00}
- Three copies: [*trisomy 21*]{color=#003FFF}

Homework notation: *47,+21,XY* -- same example, different order

=== layout: section

# Summary

=== layout: reference

# For Reference: Address Ranges

@body

- A single [*band*]{color=#003FFF}: [*17*]{color=#D40000}[*q*]{color=#B74300}[*1*]{color=#007A00}[*2*]{color=#003FFF}
- A range of [*bands*]{color=#003FFF}: [*17*]{color=#D40000}[*q*]{color=#B74300}[*1*]{color=#007A00}[*2*]{color=#003FFF}-[*q*]{color=#B74300}[*2*]{color=#007A00}[*1*]{color=#003FFF}
- A range gives a broader location when the position is less precisely known
- Decimal digits name finer [*subbands*]{color=#A719DB}; they are not decimal distances

=== layout: bookend

# Key Takeaways

@body

- [*p*]{color=#B74300}: short arm; [*q*]{color=#B74300}: long arm
- [*Address*]{color=#24578F}: [*chromosome*]{color=#D40000}, [*arm*]{color=#B74300}, [*region*]{color=#007A00}, [*band*]{color=#003FFF}, [*subband*]{color=#A719DB}
- Same [*arm*]{color=#B74300}: higher [*band*]{color=#003FFF} numbers farther from the centromere
- [*Karyotype*]{color=#24578F}: total, sex chromosomes, chromosome change

